---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About ListLift"
  description="Why we built ListLift: a multi-marketplace, evidence-based, claim-safe ecommerce listing platform that shows its homework."
>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top: var(--space-8); max-width: 780px;">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">About</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>About ListLift</h1>
    <div class="card" style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px;">
      <p>
        Writing one strong marketplace listing by hand takes 20–40 minutes: researching competitors, checking character and UTF-8 byte limits, and rewriting everything for each channel.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most AI writers hide their research and invent product features that put sellers at risk of listing suppression. ListLift was built around one simple rule: <strong>show your homework</strong>.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:0;">
        Every marketplace rule lives in a versioned, human-verified file with a visible verification date. Every factual claim traces back to your locked product facts or cited competitor data. ListLift saves labour and reduces errors — it never promises fake "#1 rankings".
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
